### Goal Model Summary

| Goal ID | Goal Title | Goal Text | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation | Justification |
|--------|------------|-----------|--------------------|-----------|----------|---------------|
| G1     | Fulfill Resource Request | Ensure resources are collected and delivered as per request. | - | Achieve | - | The mission's primary objective is to achieve the delivery of resources. |
| G2     | Collection | Collect resources from storage. | - | Perform | G1 -> G2 (AND) | Collection is a necessary step before delivery. |
| G3     | Delivery | Deliver collected resources. | - | Perform | G1 -> G3 (AND) | Delivery is the final step after collection. |
| G2.1   | Single Robot Collection | Single robot collects resources from one storage. | - | Perform | G2 -> G2.1 (OR) | Either single or multi-robot collection can fulfill the goal. |
| G2.2   | Multi-Robot Collection | Multiple robots collect resources from different storages. | - | Perform | G2 -> G2.2 (OR) | Multiple robots can handle different storages concurrently. |
| G3.1   | Single Robot Delivery | Single robot delivers resources to the destination. | - | Perform | G3 -> G3.1 (OR) | Either single or multi-robot delivery can fulfill the goal. |
| G3.2   | Multi-Robot Delivery | Multiple robots deliver resources to the destination. | - | Perform | G3 -> G3.2 (OR) | Multiple robots can handle delivery more efficiently. |
| G4     | Battery Fallback | Handle low battery situations during collection or delivery. | - | Perform | G1 -> G4 (FALLBACK) | Fallback in case of battery issues to ensure mission completion or alert. |

### Task Model Summary

| Task ID | Task Title | Task Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots | Justification |
|---------|------------|-----------|----------|----------|-------------------|---------------|
| AT2.1   | Visit Storage | Navigate to the storage location. | Sequential AND | Storage location | 1 | Single robot performs the visit. |
| AT2.2   | Request Resources | Send request to storage for resources. | Sequential AND | Storage location | 1 | Single robot handles the request. |
| AT2.3   | Move Resources | Transport resources from storage. | Sequential AND | Storage to checkpoint | 1 | Single robot moves resources. |
| AT2.4   | Multi-Robot Collection | Multiple robots collect from different storages. | Parallel AND | Multiple storage locations | [1, n] | Multiple robots work concurrently. |
| AT3.1   | Deliver Resources | Transport resources to destination. | Sequential AND | Delivery location | 1 | Single robot delivers resources. |
| AT3.2   | Multi-Robot Delivery | Multiple robots deliver resources. | Parallel AND | Delivery location | [1, n] | Multiple robots handle delivery. |
| AT4.1   | Return to Recharge | Return to recharging station. | Sequential AND | Recharge station | 1 | Low battery handling. |
| AT4.2   | Assign Mission | Assign mission to another robot. | Sequential AND | Any location | [1, n] | Ensure mission continuation. |
| AT4.3   | Return to Checkpoint | Return resources to checkpoint. | Sequential AND | Checkpoint | 1 | Low battery during delivery. |
| AT4.4   | Trigger Alert | Raise alert for failed return. | Sequential AND | Any location | 1 | Critical failure handling. |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3 (AND)**  
  Justification: Both collection and delivery are necessary for the mission to be successful.

- **G2 -> G2.1, G2.2 (OR)**  
  Justification: Either a single robot or multiple robots can collect resources, depending on the situation.

- **G2.1 -> AT2.1, AT2.2, AT2.3 (AND)**  
  Justification: These tasks must be performed sequentially for single robot collection.

- **G2.2 -> AT2.4 (AND)**  
  Justification: Multiple robots work in parallel to collect resources from different storages.

- **G3 -> G3.1, G3.2 (OR)**  
  Justification: Either a single robot or multiple robots can deliver resources.

- **G3.1 -> AT3.1 (AND)**  
  Justification: Single robot delivers resources sequentially.

- **G3.2 -> AT3.2 (AND)**  
  Justification: Multiple robots deliver resources in parallel.

- **G1 -> G4 (FALLBACK)**  
  Justification: If battery issues arise, fallback to handle low battery scenarios.

- **G4 -> AT4.1, AT4.2 (OR)**  
  Justification: Either return to recharge or assign the mission to another robot.

- **AT4.2 -> AT4.3, AT4.4 (OR)**  
  Justification: If mission assignment fails, trigger an alert.
